// FILE: transport_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: TRANSPORT-LAW
 * NAME: TRANSPORT-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Data Movement and Transfer Rules
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/transport_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define how data is transferred, routed, and delivered between modules,
 * components, and AI entities within the AVIS ecosystem.
 *
 * [TRANSPORT PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Explicit Routing:
 *    All data transfers must specify source, destination, and format.
 *
 * 2. Predictable Flow:
 *    Data should move through well-defined channels without ambiguity.
 *
 * 3. Format Stability:
 *    Data structures must remain consistent across transfers.
 *
 * 4. Integrity:
 *    Data must not be altered during transport unless explicitly requested.
 *
 * [CHANNEL TYPES]
 * - DIRECT: Module-to-module transfer.
 * - BUFFERED: Data stored temporarily before delivery.
 * - BROADCAST: Data sent to multiple receivers.
 * - REQUEST/RESPONSE: Standard query/return pattern.
 *
 * [MESSAGE REQUIREMENTS]
 * Each transport message must include:
 *   - SOURCE
 *   - DESTINATION
 *   - FORMAT
 *   - PAYLOAD
 *
 * [ERROR HANDLING]
 * If transport fails:
 *   - Return a clear error message.
 *   - Do not retry unless instructed.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All data movement must follow this law to maintain consistency and clarity.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
